---
// Placed directly after "How it works", because that section is where a
// newcomer decides the game looks complicated - six special cards, stacking,
// countering, a reverse and a suit nomination. The answer already exists in
// the app and was only mentioned on the support page, which nobody reads
// before buying.
---

<section class="learn">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2>Learn as you play</h2>
      <p>
        The tutorial deals you a hand and walks you through the special cards.
        Try an attack, answer a skip and see what happens when you change the suit.
      </p>
      <p class="aside">
        And when a card can't be played, the app says why rather than just
        refusing the tap.
      </p>
    </div>

    <img
      src="/images/shot-tutorial.webp"
      alt="The tutorial mid-lesson, explaining a special card with a real hand dealt"
      width="400"
      height="869"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .learn {
    background: var(--felt-surface);
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 3.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  p {
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .aside {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  img {
    width: min(230px, 100%);
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 1.4rem;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 7px #1c1c1e, 0 0 0 9px #3a3a3c,
      0 20px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .container {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      justify-items: center;
      text-align: center;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }
    p { margin-inline: auto; }
  }
</style>
